        "@id": "prototype:99aa373e-e2d8-490c-b331-62aa287c1cba",
        "rdfs:label": "Lalo Salamanca",
        "rdfs:comment": "Eduardo \"Lalo\" Salamanca is a fictional character and one of the main antagonists in the AMC television series Better Call Saul, a spinoff of Breaking Bad. He is portrayed by Tony Dalton, with the character being created by Peter Gould and screenwriter Gordon Smith. Lalo is introduced in the show's fourth season but was originally mentioned in dialogue from the Breaking Bad episode \"Better Call Saul\" that introduces Saul Goodman, though Lalo does not appear in the series.",
        "name": "Lalo Salamanca",
        "description": "Eduardo \"Lalo\" Salamanca is a fictional character and one of the main antagonists in the AMC television series Better Call Saul, a spinoff of Breaking Bad. He is portrayed by Tony Dalton, with the character being created by Peter Gould and screenwriter Gordon Smith. Lalo is introduced in the show's fourth season but was originally mentioned in dialogue from the Breaking Bad episode \"Better Call Saul\" that introduces Saul Goodman, though Lalo does not appear in the series.",
